{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS5MEGgevncL5hfCJB4F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job has been running every night; it failed each time, and the failure also stopped it from telling you. `launchctl print` shows 6 runs, all ending with exit code 1. The error log shows the same two lines for every run.\n\n1. **The login fails.** `claude -p` says \"Not logged in\" under launchd. The plist only gives the job `PATH`, so the CLI can't find your keychain login without `USER` set. I fixed this by adding `USER`, `LOGNAME` and `HOME` to the plist's `EnvironmentVariables`.\n2. **`status=$?` kills the script, which is why you got nothing.** In zsh, `status` is a read-only variable, and assigning to it exits the script with code 1. That line runs before either Telegram call, so even a successful review would never have been sent. I confirmed this with `zsh -c 'status=1'` and changed it to `rc=$?`.\n\nI also made it harder for the job to go silent again:\n- The prompt now goes in on stdin.\n- An empty output file counts as a failure, even when `claude` exits 0.\n- Each run logs its start time, exit code and duration.\n- All Telegram messages go through a wrapper that writes to the log if sending fails.\n- `notify.sh` now treats HTTP errors from Telegram as failures (`curl --fail-with-body`); before, a bad token or chat id was ignored.\n\n**What I tested:** the plist passes `plutil -lint` and both scripts pass a syntax check. I ran the new script with stand-ins for `claude` and `notify.sh` in three cases: login failure, success, and exit 0 with no output. Each sent the right message and exited with the right code. I couldn't test the real launchd, keychain or Telegram path from this snapshot. The plist hardcodes the username `vk`.\n\n**What you need to do on the Mac:**\n1. Copy the files into place and reload the job with `bootout` then `bootstrap`. Editing the plist alone won't pick up the new environment.\n2. Run it now with `launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review`.\n3. Check that the exit code is 0, today's review file exists and isn't empty, the run took a plausible time (not about a second), and the summary arrived on Telegram.\n4. Break it once on purpose and confirm the failure message arrives.\n\nANSWER.md has the full explanation, these steps, and which parts of your colleague's note applied. From the note, the `status` bug, the missing `USER`, checking `launchctl print` first, and \"exit 0 isn't proof it worked\" all applied. Its prompt-not-received and stdin-hang problems don't show up in your log; I piped the prompt in anyway as a precaution."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1935,"cache_read_input_tokens":28112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1935},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c9bc008-6a29-4ffe-99f4-b922331bffb8","uuid":"7ab68d56-7bd1-4fed-bb59-b916f7bc0b6d","timestamp":"2026-10-27T04:01:54.595Z","request_id":"req_011CgS5ME2nSpLmNdBx7NSq6"}
